From: QNN EP team <noreply@qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 09 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] session: deduplicate custom-op domains for AutoEP devices

AutoEP can expose multiple devices backed by the same EP factory. Each device
can return the same custom-op domain, such as the QNN qti_aisw domain.

Single-device AutoEP sessions work without this patch. For a multi-device
session, ORT collects each device's domains and registers them together in one
session-local custom registry. Registering qti_aisw twice makes
RegisterOpSet fail with "Domain already set in registry". Deduplicate domains
within that collection before registering the session's custom registry.

---
diff --git a/onnxruntime/core/session/utils.cc b/onnxruntime/core/session/utils.cc
index 8fc6c1d8c0..8d3a79740d 100644
--- a/onnxruntime/core/session/utils.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/session/utils.cc
@@ -318,7 +318,10 @@ static OrtStatus* CreateSessionAndLoadSingleModelImpl(_In_ const OrtSessionOptio
       ORT_API_RETURN_IF_STATUS_NOT_OK(GetCustomOpDomainsFromEpDevice(*ep_device, domains));
 
       for (auto domain : domains) {
-        if (ShouldAddDomain(domain, options->custom_op_domains_)) {
+        // Multiple EP devices can expose the same custom-op domain. Keep one copy
+        // in this session's collection before its custom registry is created.
+        if (ShouldAddDomain(domain, options->custom_op_domains_) &&
+            ShouldAddDomain(domain, all_ep_custom_op_domains)) {
           all_ep_custom_op_domains.push_back(domain);
         }
       }
@@ -431,7 +434,10 @@ static OrtStatus* CreateSessionAndLoadModelImpl(_In_ const OrtSessionOptions* op
       ORT_API_RETURN_IF_STATUS_NOT_OK(GetCustomOpDomainsFromEpDevice(*ep_device, domains));
 
       for (auto domain : domains) {
-        if (ShouldAddDomain(domain, options->custom_op_domains_)) {
+        // Multiple EP devices can expose the same custom-op domain. Keep one copy
+        // in this session's collection before its custom registry is created.
+        if (ShouldAddDomain(domain, options->custom_op_domains_) &&
+            ShouldAddDomain(domain, all_ep_custom_op_domains)) {
           all_ep_custom_op_domains.push_back(domain);
         }
       }
